# GitPrompt's environment profiles (tools/env.mjs). The `just` recipes and `just quality` load, in
# this order (later wins): .env, .env.local, .env.<profile>, .env.<profile>.local. A variable set in
# your shell wins over all of them. Committed: .env and .env.<profile>. Yours: the *.local files.
#
#   development  `just dev`, `just desktop-dev`                   .env.development
#   production   `just serve`, `just build`, the installed app     .env.production
#   performance  `just perf`, `just bench`, the timing reports      .env.performance
#
# The binaries never read these files: an installed app runs in production unless GITPROMPT_ENV says
# otherwise. Every variable is documented where it is read (backend/crates/gitprompt-core/src/settings.rs,
# backend/crates/gitprompt-server/src/logging.rs, backend/apps/desktop/src/perf/config.rs).
#
# Shared by every profile:
# GITPROMPT_LOG_FORMAT=json
